Current original Zero workflow (0.12)

Use the native tools on Linux or their .exe versions on Windows:
  zero-integrate PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_KERNEL.zero
  zero-build PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY NEW_KERNEL.zero
  zero-check PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_TEST_DIRECTORY
All destination paths must be new. The integrator preserves authored sources;
the builder checks its compiler fixed point and builds the original targets;
the verifier checks language behavior and host file operations in process.
See tools/integrate.ztext, tools/build.ztext and checks/README.ztext.
Read these documents with zero-text read FILE.

The notes below preserve earlier implementation and test history. Any old
shell/Python runner names, generated artifacts, JSON reports or commands are
historical references: they were removed from the active project and are not
current runnable instructions or current-release validation. Native host
checks do not replace BIOS/UEFI, persistence or physical-hardware testing.

Historical implementation notes

Original Zero keyboard applications (canonical0.10)

apps opens the one-based keyboard menu; system, storage and network open
individual applications. Arrow keys select; Enter opens/applies. Backspace
returns to the application menu, and Escape restores the terminal. The
network application can enter the existing honest hardware WiFi interface.

System reports the existing terminal/graphics/computation worker states and
can pause/resume computation. Network polling remains scheduled independently.
Storage lists actual discovered volumes and selects a separate volume root;
it does not create, resize, format, mount or modify filesystems. Network
shows the actual driver/DHCP state and its address, mask, gateway and DNS.
These are bounded keyboard applications, not a new process isolation model.

Implementation is in the three original .zero.part files. The NET integrator
expands only approved APP names, after expanding approved NET parts once.
apps/integrate.py checks this canonical integration or exports a source snapshot.
Product behavior and rendering are Zero; integration scripts are host tooling.
All state lives in existing owned console fields2472/2480/2488, and rendering
reuses the bounded45-column by12-row modal frame. The candidate header fix
keeps its APPLICATION glyph length11, preventing an over-read of the label.

Functionally tested source261936 bytes (208 below limit262144); its exact
source/binaries are retained in verification/apps-next/tested-*.
